    "text": "A long Navy career\nThe Algol was an attack cargo ship, a kind of Navy ship designed to carry troops and supplies for landings from the sea. It was launched in 1943 as the James Barnes, but soon renamed Algol, after a star in the constellation of Perseus. It served in the Pacific during World War II and remained a commissioned Navy ship for more than 22 years. Then the ship sat in storage for years.",
